":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120607","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-06-24T18:54:04Z"},{"id":4835330347,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIDVJKw","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"8f003177ddb08f4e2de961103e02ecdb5f4f28e9","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","login":"lyuma","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma"},"body":"Approved in animation meeting. My opinion is that this should not be considered compat breaking.\n\nThere is no case where the serialized transform of a valid BoneAttachment3D should be used after deserialization, and therefore there is no reason to serialize it, which is exactly what this PR changes\n\nThe specific update order of bone attachments relative to scene entering the tree is something I would consider an implementation detail, so it should be okay to change.\n\nThe only usecase that could be considered compat breaking would be if someone needs to serialize then deserialize the scene, then inspect the BoneAttachment3D transform. I do not know of anyone who needs this usecase, not even gltf export (which ignores BoneAttachment3D transforms). So I would merge this and someone needs to justify their usecase if we need ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120607#pullrequestreview-4835330347","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120607","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-08-01T18:06:21Z"}]